<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The hardened runtime's exceptions for a Developer ID build (build/signing.cjs). Unused while the
     build is signed ad hoc. The same list goes on the app and, as entitlementsInherit, on everything
     inside it, including the bundled engine's interpreter (Contents/Resources/engine/bin/Tearsheet
     Engine), which the app starts as a child process.

     - allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 (Electron) writes machine code at run time.
       CPython's ctypes/libffi closures need writable-then-executable memory too.
     - disable-library-validation: the engine loads its Python extension modules (.so files in
       site-packages) and libpython from Resources. They are re-signed with the same Team ID, but
       some wheels ship their own dylibs; without this a single one of them stops the engine.
     - allow-dyld-environment-variables is NOT set: nothing needs DYLD_*.

     Network access, the Keychain and starting Terminal with /usr/bin/open need no entitlement
     outside the App Sandbox, which Tearsheet doesn't use. Tighten this once a signed build has run
     end to end (docs/launch/signing.md, "After the first signed build"). -->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
